==Special Moves==
====Cross Diving====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Cross Diving
|moveId=mrbig_236b,mrbig_236d,mrbig_236bd
|input=236B/D/BD
|input2=qcf+B/D/BD
|description3=Soar straight forward into the opponent with a horizontal dive.
* Can be braked at any point after the first active frame to cancel the rest of the flight and immediately enter recovery frames
* Mostly very unsafe (can be mitigated with extremely accurate spacing, attempting to utilize this is not recommended), but has very long range and launches on counterhit.
* Launches on counterhit
* Can be used to bypass these projectiles by flying over/through it. Anything not listed here can hit Mr Big during the flight.
** Rock's Reppuken (All versions)
** Terry's Power Wave (A/C versions)
** B. Jenet's Baffles (All versions)
** Hokutomaru's Shuriken (Regular versions, the move's hitbox destroys the projectiles)
----
'''Light version (236B)'''
* Fastest startup, but shortest range
* While 623K and 214K are better Guard Cancel options in many situations, 236B is a great option in its own right with powerful, niche applications where it can shine, such as to launch the counterhit recovery state of a braked anti-air (especially Kain flashkick) and Billy's Far C special cancels from long range
----
'''Heavy version (236D)'''
* Slowest startup, better range than the light version
* Still fast enough to launch a braked anti-air if used as a guard cancel, but too slow to punish most other attacks
----
'''Rev version (236BD)'''
* Same range as the heavy version, but slightly faster startup (still slower than the light version)
* Can be made safe on block (or start a combo on hit) by canceling into another Rev special, making it a solid option for approaching the opponent
}}

====Crazy Drum====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Crazy Drum
|moveId=mrbig_214b,mrbig_214d,mrbig_214bd
|input=214B/D/BD
|input2=qcb+B/D/BD
|description3=A rapid, 4-hit attack with short range. A versatile special attack with many different use cases.
----
'''Light version (214B):'''
Mr Big’s fastest strike special. Used to end blockstrings safely and as combo filler, but can also be used as a light confirm.
* Mr Big’s most reliable special attack for Guard Cancels at close range. Use 236B instead if the opponent is too far.
* Any special-cancelable normal can combo into this, if Mr Big is close enough. 
* Can only start/extend a combo if it hits an airborne/juggled opponent, or as counterhit / Wild Punish.

----
'''Heavy version (214D)'''
Used to convert heavy attack hits into big damage.
* Slower and just barely unsafe on block, but launches the opponent just enough to start a combo on hit.
* Any special-cancelable heavy attack can combo into this, assuming the opponent is close enough. On hit, combos into 623C (brake).

----
'''Rev version (214BD)'''
Used as combo filler.
* Slower than the light version, but faster than the heavy version. Adds a fifth hit, but can be braked to stop on the fourth and remain safe on block.
* Although the final hit is unsafe on block, it can be canceled into another Rev special, keeping Mr Big safe at the cost of additional Rev meter.

}}

