====Ground Blaster====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=mrbig_236A,mrbig_236C,mrbig_236AC
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|description3=Fire a projectile along the ground. Will not actually travel fullscreen unless Rev meter is spent.
* Light and heavy versions have a close-range hitbox that is only active for 2 frames with better damage and advantage on block than the projectile. It also knocks the opponent down on hit.
* The numbers in [brackets] represent values for the close-range hitbox (exact range is very slightly shorter than 1 forward hop).

----
'''Light version (236A)'''
* Shortest range, will hit from slightly shorter than round start distance
* The short range hitbox will launch on counterhit, a projectile counterhit stumbles the opponent for 32 frames
----
'''Heavy version (236C)'''
* Slower startup, but better damage, advantage on block/hit, and range (will hit from slightly further than round-start)
* The short range hitbox will launch on counterhit, a projectile counterhit stumbles the opponent for 35 frames
* Can be used as a frame-trap tool if canceled into from Close C
----
'''Rev version (236AC)'''
* Fires a fullscreen projectile along the ground, but does not include the close-range hitbox that the normal versions have and will never launch on counterhit (stumbles opponent for 38 frames)
* Same startup as the light version with better damage on the projectile, and is always at least +2 on block
}}

====California Romance====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=California Romance
|moveId=mrbig_623a,mrbig_623c,mrbig_623ac
|input=623A/C/AC
|input2=dp+A/C/AC
|display=200x200px
|description3=
Mr. Big leaps and swipes a baton upwards with his main arm. Used primarily as anti-air and combo filler. Does not launch on counterhit '''unless''' the first hit whiffs and the second hit lands as a counterhit, and 623A will not recover fast enough to start a combo in this situation.
----
'''Light version (623A):'''
* '''This is not fully invulnerable during startup (or ever). Do not use this as a reversal.''' It is, however, immediately invulnerable to air attacks through all of its startup and first half of its active frames. 
* Mr Big's fastest anti-air, and it hits twice
* Hits from slightly shorter than round-start distance, or the distance of a full jump
----
'''Heavy version (623C):'''
* Adds a long dash before attacking. Despite retaining air-invulnerability, this is way too slow to be used as an anti-air, and so it is mostly used as combo filler.
* Can be braked at two different points:
** If braked during the startup dash on the ground, immediately enters recovery frames after 9 frames of air-invulnerable dashing
** Otherwise, can be braked right as the attack becomes active to stop Mr Big from going airborne and cancel the third hit. This is still barely punishable on block, unlike other braked anti-air specials.
----
'''Rev version (623AC):'''
* Slightly slower than the light version, but with longer range. It is still fast enough to combo from any special-cancelable attack, making it an excellent tool for starting combos from lights.
* Has the same two brake points as the heavy version, but is actually safe on block
* Braked version launches the opponent higher than the braked heavy version
}}

