==Super Special Moves==
====Blaster Wave====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Blaster Wave
|moveId=mrbig_236236A,mrbig_236236C
|input=236236A/C
|input2=qcfqcf+A/C
|description2=
* Because this move spawns a projectile and is not a strike move "connected" to Mr. Big himself, JDing all of the hits of the move causes the extra JD stop frames to delay the blockstun of this move beyond normal amounts, resulting in a frame advantage for him to what would normally be about -30.
** This creates a win-win situation for Mr. Big if this is used as an anti-air: if it hits, it hits. If it gets JD'd, the opponent will have to JD all the remaining hits in order to not take damage, but doing so probably results in it being safe or even plus for Mr. Big.
}}

====Rising Spear====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Rising Spear
|moveId=mrbig_236236B,mrbig_236236D
|input=236236B/D
|input2=qcfqcf+B/D
|description2=Spend super meter to launch a beefed-up command grab. Very high damage, fully invulnerable and can function as a reversal. Same range as 623K.
* Also great for use as a Guard Cancel during an opponent’s blockstring, unless the opponent is using a long-range attack (e.g. Billy Far C blockstrings)
* The slower startup of the 1-bar version ('''236236B''') allows it to beat safejumps.
* For the extra meter spent, the 2-bar version ('''236236D''') is faster and deals more damage. Using it as a Guard Cancel on wakeup will scale the damage for no benefit at all (it is already active and invulnerable on frame 1), and should be avoided.
}}

